  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-1",
      "transcript": "Why can a hotter pan make a drop of water last longer?",
      "start": 0,
      "duration": 3.159583,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.4c3220bfa3d5e9844bf96ce3c1a9d9f99a826bc92127748834a0cc61f51d6036",
        "sha256": "4c3220bfa3d5e9844bf96ce3c1a9d9f99a826bc92127748834a0cc61f51d6036"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-2",
      "transcript": "On a hot metal surface, water can touch the metal and boil away quickly.",
      "start": 3.5,
      "duration": 4.233375,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.561f80d78ce734fcf613813dce49d4b7a00ca2c423878ee6ad2ea0043b90a567",
        "sha256": "561f80d78ce734fcf613813dce49d4b7a00ca2c423878ee6ad2ea0043b90a567"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-3",
      "transcript": "Heat it far enough, and something changes.",
      "start": 8,
      "duration": 2.236875,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.a343ebfed2822f1e095d42752114d8af84a86cc129bb00cd188a3430b1694c09",
        "sha256": "a343ebfed2822f1e095d42752114d8af84a86cc129bb00cd188a3430b1694c09"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-4",
      "transcript": "The bottom of the drop turns to vapor almost instantly.",
      "start": 10.5,
      "duration": 3.149333,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.5d4581a89a4e8d6dc0b5f9f8a1d92861b84f462e58ef6307ff12d2a5f7acbaa2",
        "sha256": "5d4581a89a4e8d6dc0b5f9f8a1d92861b84f462e58ef6307ff12d2a5f7acbaa2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-5",
      "transcript": "That vapor forms a cushion, lifting the rest of the water off the metal.",
      "start": 13.9,
      "duration": 3.833917,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.607844ce99c82d04e39d2a9e1527e00ae6f19e9207ef2facb586943782a45a3c",
        "sha256": "607844ce99c82d04e39d2a9e1527e00ae6f19e9207ef2facb586943782a45a3c"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-6",
      "transcript": "Now heat must cross a poorly conducting gas layer.",
      "start": 18.1,
      "duration": 2.927208,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.942abc8f21cff9e052ed35224e03d80eec1698277d9054b48a74d2507b92f8cc",
        "sha256": "942abc8f21cff9e052ed35224e03d80eec1698277d9054b48a74d2507b92f8cc"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-7",
      "transcript": "The hotter surface has created a barrier to its own heat.",
      "start": 21.266666666666666,
      "duration": 3.110708,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.94f92e7c9c250f3872f7713e3d6c63c63878c93f7e6c00c4f646f1d491e724f6",
        "sha256": "94f92e7c9c250f3872f7713e3d6c63c63878c93f7e6c00c4f646f1d491e724f6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-8",
      "transcript": "This is the Leidenfrost effect.",
      "start": 24.766666666666666,
      "duration": 1.975292,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.b33a0b25b2dab7de68d0bf28427d1a138e5f6e155c06ccd6b347c9e1c8b16cfd",
        "sha256": "b33a0b25b2dab7de68d0bf28427d1a138e5f6e155c06ccd6b347c9e1c8b16cfd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-9",
      "transcript": "It doesn’t mean hotter always makes water last longer.",
      "start": 27,
      "duration": 2.849417,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.9443a4b3f8d2eec0bdd0bfd34d60a3f9ed4eaa6c7b9334cb56c43fa4781a67ba",
        "sha256": "9443a4b3f8d2eec0bdd0bfd34d60a3f9ed4eaa6c7b9334cb56c43fa4781a67ba"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-10",
      "transcript": "The transition depends on the surface and the drop.",
      "start": 30.1,
      "duration": 3.011125,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.8a00dfd999a8a6d951af001b2ced98f3db3e0a179b878bc41d64a3bbe91f8d06",
        "sha256": "8a00dfd999a8a6d951af001b2ced98f3db3e0a179b878bc41d64a3bbe91f8d06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-11",
      "transcript": "Above it, more heat can speed evaporation again.",
      "start": 33.36666666666667,
      "duration": 2.858167,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.d959508a90fbef3cfacaf97a59e52110386283594f37320d637e45508988ce7d",
        "sha256": "d959508a90fbef3cfacaf97a59e52110386283594f37320d637e45508988ce7d"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-12",
      "transcript": "The surprise is that a hotter surface can give water less direct contact with the heat.",
      "start": 36.46666666666667,
      "duration": 4.927,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.4b41a1bf63c7b570183c526156231197f9315a6a7cd22ead503e2acf5fe691e7",
        "sha256": "4b41a1bf63c7b570183c526156231197f9315a6a7cd22ead503e2acf5fe691e7"
      }
    }
  ],
